          "The relational gospel shares the Reformed stress on God’s initiative and the Wesleyan stress on real, free response. It frames the issue relationally: love always comes first (1 John 4:19), and love invites, it does not force. God’s initiative is not a cold decree but the Father’s embrace in Jesus, already given. Our response is not a work that earns, but a child’s trust that receives. The question “who does what?” matters less than “who is this God who comes to us?”"
