        "text": "<em>Palingenesia</em> (from <em>palin</em>, “again”, and <em>genesis</em>, “birth”) appears only twice in the New Testament: Matthew 19:28, of the renewal of all things when the Son of Man sits on his throne, and Titus 3:5, “the washing of regeneration”. Thayer notes the word commonly denotes “the restoration of a thing to its pristine state, its renovation”.",
